  "authoringNote": "Two current, usable, final orders with different document IDs and no supersession state different order dates (2026-09-01 and 2026-09-04) and agree on every other element, including the signed date 2026-09-05, which is held equal so that only the order-date field disagrees. SPEC F14 requires the conflict to remain and forbids confidence from choosing a winner. R03 compares every current usable order and holds one R03.orders_disagree with field order.date naming both orders; R04 compares final current usable orders and holds one R04.orders_disagree with field order.date naming both; each is a conflict for the administrative reviewer, and neither selects a date. Each encounter and order pair is otherwise in sequence (12 and 15 days after the 2026-08-20 encounter), within the C01 bound 2027-02-20 and shares SYN-PRAC-0001, so no pairwise chronology or identity condition holds, and no signature-date or encounter-date disagreement exists. Every order has its own linked receipt after its order date span (A: 2026-08-31T10:00Z to 2026-09-02T12:00Z, receipt 2026-09-06T17:00:00Z; B: 2026-09-03T10:00Z to 2026-09-05T12:00Z, receipt 2026-09-06T18:00:00Z), so R05 passes (C06, C09) and no unrelated gap is accidental. Citations: R01 seven supplier fields and both order codes (9); R02 beneficiary name and identifier of the encounter, both orders and both receipts (10); R03 all nine element facts of each order (18); R04 the encounter status, date and practitioner identifier and each order's status, date and practitioner identifier (9); R05 both receipts' reference and time fields and both order dates (8); R06 five clinical statements; R07 the false LCMP flag. No parent is named (C07). R08 and R09 pass and R10 is not applicable. The state is needs_human_review. Distinct from F14x1 (encounter dates), F14x2 (several simultaneous conditions) and F14x3 (draft beside final order, R03 only).",
